                <pb facs="0299" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9311/322: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-15T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>188. During diplomatic hours yesterday the Chinese Minister, Alfred Sze, called
                    on me without appointment and informed me of the receipt by him of a cable from
                    the Nationalist Government inquiring as to his willingness to continue as
                    “China’s representative” in Washington. I was informed by Sze that his reply was
                    in the affirmative. I merely thanked him for the information and made no
                    comment. There was no further conversation beyond this.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
